{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfrv9W2TapBtyVwfmAxWP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"<REDACTED>","signature":""},{"type":"server_tool_use","id":"srvtoolu_01LLbAiUudS3cYmMBo6SL1BL","name":"web_search","input":{"query":"Claude Code overview documentation Anthropic"}},{"type":"web_search_tool_result","tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01LLbAiUudS3cYmMBo6SL1BL","content":[{"type":"web_search_result","title":"Claude Code Official Documentation by Anthropic","url":"https://claudelog.com/faqs/claude-code-docs/","encrypted_content":"","page_age":"412 days ago"},{"type":"web_search_result","title":"claude-code-analysis/DOCUMENTATION.md at main · ComeOnOliver/claude-code-analysis","url":"https://github.com/ComeOnOliver/claude-code-analysis/blob/main/DOCUMENTATION.md","encrypted_content":"","page_age":"192 days ago"},{"type":"web_search_result","title":"Overview - Claude Code Docs","url":"https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/agents-and-tools/claude-code/overview","encrypted_content":"","page_age":"525 days ago"},{"type":"web_search_result","title":"GitHub - anthropics/claude-code: Claude Code is an agentic coding tool that lives in your terminal, understands your codebase, and helps you code faster by executing routine tasks, explaining complex code, and handling git workflows - all through natural language commands. · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code","encrypted_content":"","page_age":"6 days ago"},{"type":"web_search_result","title":"The Claude Code Handbook: A Professional Introduction to Building with AI-Assisted Development","url":"https://www.freecodecamp.org/news/claude-code-handbook/","encrypted_content":"","page_age":"197 days ago"},{"type":"web_search_result","title":"Overview - Claude Code Docs","url":"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/overview","encrypted_content":"","page_age":"86 days ago"},{"type":"web_search_result","title":"Claude Code by Anthropic","url":"https://claude.com/product/claude-code","encrypted_content":"","page_age":"0 days ago"},{"type":"web_search_result","title":"Documentation - Claude Platform Docs","url":"https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/home","encrypted_content":"","page_age":"183 days ago"},{"type":"web_search_result","title":"Claude Code","url":"https://aiagentindex.mit.edu/2025/claude-code","encrypted_content":"","page_age":null}],"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"<REDACTED>","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I searched for \"Claude Code overview documentation Anthropic.\" Here's what came up:\n\n## Where the official docs are\nThe official overview page appears to be at **code.claude.com/docs/en/overview**. That's the docs link in Anthropic's `anthropics/claude-code` GitHub repo, which was updated about 6 days ago "},{"citations":[],"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"text","text":". Older sources, like a ClaudeLog page from more than a year ago, link to "},{"citations":[],"type":"text","text":"https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code/overview"},{"type":"text","text":" instead. The docs.anthropic.com version also appeared in the results with the same title and content, so the docs have probably just moved to the new domain.\n\n## What Claude Code is\n- "},{"citations":[],"type":"text","text":"The overview calls it an agentic coding tool. It reads your codebase, edits files, runs commands, and connects to your development tools. You can use it in a terminal, an IDE, the desktop app, or a browser."},{"type":"text","text":"\n- "},{"citations":[],"type":"text","text":"You can also tag @claude on GitHub."},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n## Where it runs and how to get access\n- "},{"citations":[],"type":"text","text":"The docs have getting-started tabs for Terminal, VS Code, the Desktop app, Web, and JetBrains."},{"type":"text","text":"\n- "},{"citations":[],"type":"text","text":"Most of these need a Claude subscription or an Anthropic Console account. The Terminal CLI, VS Code, and JetBrains can also use third-party providers."},{"type":"text","text":"\n- "},{"citations":[],"type":"text","text":"Access comes with Claude Pro, Max, Team, or Enterprise plans, or with a Claude Console account."},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n## Installing it (from the docs)\n- "},{"citations":[],"type":"text","text":"The recommended way is the native install."},{"type":"text","text":" You can also use Homebrew or WinGet. "},{"citations":[],"type":"text","text":"WinGet installs don't update themselves, so you need to run `winget upgrade Anthropic.ClaudeCode` now and then."},{"type":"text","text":"\n- "},{"citations":[],"type":"text","text":"On Linux, you can install with apt, dnf, or apk (Debian, Fedora, RHEL, and Alpine)."},{"type":"text","text":"\n- To start it, go to your project folder and run `claude`. "},{"citations":[],"type":"text","text":"It asks you to log in the first time. If you've set the ANTHROPIC_API_KEY environment variable and approve using it, the login step is skipped."},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n## Example uses\n- "},{"citations":[],"type":"text","text":"The overview shows `claude -p` running without a chat session, for example to check piped log output for problems or to handle translations in CI and open a PR."},{"type":"text","text":"\n- The product page lists three main uses:\n  - "},{"citations":[],"type":"text","text":"Learning a new codebase. It maps the project with agentic search, so you don't have to pick context files by hand."},{"type":"text","text":"\n  - "},{"citations":[],"type":"text","text":"Turning issues into pull requests using GitHub, GitLab, and command-line tools."},{"type":"text","text":"\n  - "},{"citations":[],"type":"text","text":"Refactors and migrations that take several hours."},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n## Other sources in the results\n- **ClaudeLog** is a community site. "},{"citations":[],"type":"text","text":"It covers practical tips and best practices to go with the official docs."},{"type":"text","text":"\n- **freeCodeCamp's Claude Code Handbook** is a longer introduction. "},{"citations":[],"type":"text","text":"It says Claude Code was used inside Anthropic for four to five months before its public release."},{"type":"text","text":"\n- **MIT AI Agent Index** "},{"citations":[],"type":"text","text":"gives 24/02/2025 as the release date and 22/05/2025 as the general release date."},{"type":"text","text":"\n- **Claude Platform Docs** (platform.claude.com) "},{"citations":[],"type":"text","text":"links to Claude Code from its main developer docs page."},{"type":"text","text":"\n\nFor current details, start with the official overview at code.claude.com/docs/en/overview. "},{"citations":[],"type":"text","text":"It links to a Quickstart that walks you through a first real task."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":13224,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":6312,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":4840},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":1,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null}